-- D-205 (owner: "with all the available data in Salesforce train the Pico Bot
-- and add all the training data in AI Rules for Salesforce"): the Salesforce
-- guide (docs/AI-RULES-SALESFORCE.md) becomes the Salesforce chat rules, only when none were
-- written yet, so rules the IT team saved are never replaced. Recorded as
-- saved by the first Super Admin; a database without users (a fresh test
-- database) gets nothing. Generated by scripts/dev/write-salesforce-rules-migration.mjs.
-- @begin
INSERT INTO ai_rules (chat_mode, content, updated_by)
SELECT 'SALESFORCE', '# Salesforce guide for Pico Bot (ARS Steels)

Built 26 Oct 2026 from the ARS Salesforce setup (objects, fields, values in use). Record counts are as of that date and grow. All data is from 2026 (Salesforce went live 30 Dec 2025).

## 1. Words people use → where the data is
- **Dealer, distributor, sub-dealer, customer, party** → Account. **Dealer code** = Account.Customer_Code__c (label "Customer Code"), e.g. 1JA02. Category = Account_Type__c: 1 Distributor, 2 Dealer, 4 Sub-Dealer (group by Account_Type__c; Customer_category__c is a formula and can''t be grouped; the standard Type is unused).
- **Executive, employee, MDE, SE, field staff, team** → Employee__c (label "Executive"). Its Name is the Employee Code; the person''s name is Employee_Name__c. Salesforce logins are a different object, User (linked by Employee__c.Salesforce_User__c).
- **MDE** = Market Development Executive (Employee__c.Designation__c = ''MDE'').
- **Primary order, CO, DO, contract, dispatch, booking** → Order. **Secondary order, SO, site order, conversion** → Secondary_Order__c.
- **Region** → Region_Master__c. **District, city, town, cluster** → Cluster__c.
- **Site, construction site, project lead** → Site_Lead__c. **Dealer lead, new dealer enquiry** → Lead.
- **Mason, contractor, architect, engineer, bar-bender, loyalty member** → Influencer__c.
- **PJP** = Permanent Journey Plan (visit beat plan) → PJP_Plan__c / PJP_Line_Items__c.
- **Attendance, check-in, leave, allowance, distance travelled** → Attendance__c. **Visit, call, field visit** → Visit__c.
- **Collection, payment follow-up, dues collected** → Collection_Plan__c / Collection_Items__c. **Ledger, outstanding** → Account.Ledger_Balance__c, Account_Transactions__c, Allocation_Transactions__c.
- **Stock at dealer** → Current_Stock__c. **Competitor stock** → Dealer_Competitor__c. **Competitor brands** → Competitor__c.
- **Target vs achievement** → Dealer_Target__c (dealer tonnage), Employee_Target__c (executive activity targets), Target_Master__c (templates).
- **Invoice, billing, e-way bill** → Invoice__c / Invoice_Lines__c. **Products, sizes, grades** → Product2.
- **Scheme, incentive, credit points** → Scheme__c / Scheme_Account__c. **Loyalty points, redemption** → Loyalty_Request__c / Redemption_Request__c.
- **Branding, boards, merchandising** → Branding_Request__c. **Complaint, case** → Case. **Techvan, steel testing** → Tech_Van__c and Visit__c (Visit_Type__c = ''Techvan Visit''). **Website enquiry** → Website_Enquiry__c. **MOM, manager visit notes** → Manager_MOM__c.
- **MT** = metric tonnes (all steel quantities). **COB** = booking/price-protection window. **SSS** = secondary sales. **ROT1/ROT2** = Rest of Tamil Nadu.

## 2. Regions
9 regions (Region_Master__c.Name): Andhra Pradesh, Chennai (parent of Chennai North and Chennai South), Karnataka, Kerala, Project (not a place), ROT1, ROT2. Most objects link to a region through Region__c (Employee__c and Visit__c use Region_Master__c). Grouping by a region field gives region names. User.Region_Master__c is a text picklist mixing names and codes (AP01, BAN1, CHEN, KL01); prefer Employee__c for people by region.

## 3. Objects (key fields; values actually used)
**Account** (~90): Name, Customer_Code__c, Account_Type__c [1,2,4], Status__c [Active, Inactive, Draft], Region__c, City__c/District__c → Cluster__c, Employee__c (assigned executive) and MDE__c → Employee__c, Customer_Credit_Risk__c [Green, Orange, Red], Credit_Limit__c, Ledger_Balance__c, Payment_Due_Date__c, Pending_Order_Amount__c, Non_Invoiced_DO_Final_Order_Amount__c, Current_Year_Target__c, Current_Year_Actual__c, Previous_Year_Target__c, Previous_Year_Actual__c, Current_Year_Avg_Monthly_Sales__c, Year_to_Year_Growth__c, ARS_Share__c, Current_Month_SSS__c, Previous_Month_SSS__c, Overall_Potential__c, Login_Status__c (dealer app), DMS_Last_Login_Date__c.

**Order** (~670, primary orders to dealers, pushed to the ERP): Type [Contract Order, Dispatch Order]. A CO is the booking (with expiry); a DO is a dispatch against a CO (Contract_Order__c → its CO) and goes through approvals before invoicing. AccountId → dealer, Consignee__c → Account, Executive__c / Manager__c → Employee__c, Region__c, EffectiveDate (order start), Order_Expiry_Date__c, Order_Approved_Date__c, Order_Invoiced_Date__c, Total_Quantity__c (MT), Total_Order_Amount__c, Total_Order_Amount_With_GST__c, Payment_Mode__c [IM, AD, On Credit, Advance, Mixed], Source__c [FS APP, DMS, Dealer], Order_Punch_Status__c [Success, Failed, In-Progress] (ERP push). Status in use: CO: CO Expired (most), CO Created, Draft CO. DO: Draft DO, DO Created, DO Invoiced, Submitted For Approval, Finance Approved, DO Cancelled, Manager Approved, Awaiting Dealer Approval, DO Rejected, Dealer Rejected, ASP_BO_Approved, CL Approved, Dealer Approved, Awaiting CL Approval. Lines: OrderItem (OrderId, Product2Id, Quantity in MT, UnitPrice, TotalPrice). Order_Line__c is unused.

**Secondary_Order__c** (~750, orders booked through a dealer for a site or influencer; the dealer approves and it is "converted"): Dealer_Distributor__c → Account, Converted_Dealer_Distributor__c → Account, Executive__c / MDE__c → Employee__c, Region__c, Site__c → Site_Lead__c, Influencer__c, Item__c → Product2, Order_date__c, Conversion_Date__c, Quantity_in_MT__c, Conversion_Quantity__c, Total_Price__c, Source__c [FSE APP, Influencer APP, DMS, E-Commerce]. Status__c in use: New, Converted, Awaiting Dealer Approval, Draft, Cancelled, Order Lost, Dealer Approved, Dealer Rejected, Invoiced, Site Complete. Order_Type__c is Hot/Warm/Cold (lead temperature), NOT an order type. Lines: Secondary_Order_Line_Item__c (Product__c, Quantity__c MT, Total_Amount__c).

**Invoice__c** (~45, ERP invoices against DOs): Order__c, Dealer_Distributor__c → Account, Region__c, Invoice_Date__c, Payment_Due_Date__c, Status__c [Created, Canceled], Total_Invoice_Amount__c, Total_GST_Value__c, Total_Weight_in_MT__c. Lines: Invoice_Lines__c. Few invoices exist compared with orders; say so when comparing.

**Employee__c / Executive** (~36): Employee_Name__c, Department__c [Sales, SSS, NBD, Telecalling, Techvan, Admin, ED, EDO], Designation__c [MDE, Sales Executive, Assistant Manager, Sales Manager, Manager, BD Executive, …], Team__c, Status__c [Active, Inactive, Draft] (use Status__c = ''Active'' for active executives), Region_Master__c → region, Last_Login__c (field-app login), Date_Of_Joining__c, Reporting_Manager__c → User.

**Attendance__c** (~570, daily check-in/out and leave): Employee__c → Employee__c, Region__c, Attendance_Date__c, Attendance_Type__c [Present, Leave], Present_Type__c [Market, Office, Event, Other], Absent_Reason__c, Status__c [Completed, In progress, Open, Approval Required, Closed], Check_in_Time__c, Check_Out_Time__c, Completed_Visits__c, Distance_Traveled__c, Total_Allowance__c. "Who is present today" = Attendance_Date__c = TODAY and Attendance_Type__c = ''Present''.

**Visit__c** (~1,160): Executive__c → Employee__c, Account__c (dealer), Lead__c, Site__c, Influencer__c, Region_Master__c, Visit_date__c (some are future plans), Visit_Type__c [Site Visit, Customer Visit, Lead Visit, Influencer Visit, Techvan Visit], **Visit_Status__c** [Completed, Cancelled, Scheduled, Planned, Rescheduled, In Progress] (Status__c is legacy, ignore), Visit_Plan_Type__c [Planned, Unplanned], Visit_Outcome__c, Reason__c, Next_Followup_Date__c, Required_Quantity_In_MT__c. Here MDE__c points to User, not Employee__c.

**Site_Lead__c** (~415, construction sites): Site_Name__c, Executive__c, Dealer__c → Account, Influencer__c, Region__c, **Site_Status__c** [In Progress, Order Created, Order Completed, Site Completed, Site Lost] (the main status), Type_of_Building__c [Apartment, Commercial, Individual House, …], Construction_Stage__c, Total_Estimated_Steel_Requirement_MT__c, Immediate_Steel_Requirement_MT__c, Final_Converted_Qty__c, Next_Requirement_Date__c, ARS_Lead_Stage__c [Hot, Warm, Cold].

**Lead** (~195, prospective dealers/distributors, not sites): Company, Status in use [Open - Not Contacted (most), New, Converted, Working, Unqualified, Nurturing], Lead_Type__c [Dealer, Distributor, Sub Dealer, HUB, Spoke, Others], Rating [Hot, Warm, Cold], Executive__c, Region__c, ARS_Potential_in_MT__c, Lead_Date__c, IsConverted, ConvertedDate.

**Dealer_Target__c** (dealer tonnage targets): Dealer__c → Account, Executive__c, Start_Date__c, End_Date__c, Target__c (MT), Achieved_Target__c (MT), Status__c [Active, Draft, Inactive]. **Employee_Target__c** (executive activity targets): Assigned_To__c → Employee__c, Target_Type__c [Visit Target, Call Target, Site Lead Target, Influencer Target, Secondary Conversion Target, BTL Meet Target], Target__c, Achieved_Target__c, Start_Date__c, End_Date__c.

**Collection_Plan__c**: Customer_Dealer_Distributor__c → Account, Executive__c, Planned_Date__c, Estimated_Amount__c, Collected_Amount__c, Status__c in use [Partially Collected, Collected, Pending, In Progress, Scheduled], Mode_of_Payment__c. **Collection_Items__c**: receipts (Collection_Plan__c, Collected_Amount__c, Mode_of_Payment__c [UPI, Cash]).

**Current_Stock__c**: Dealer__c → Account, Item__c → Product2, Total_Stock_in_MT__c (stock snapshots from visits). **Dealer_Competitor__c**: Dealer__c, Competitor__c → Competitor__c, Stock__c (MT), Brand_Grade__c.

**Account_Transactions__c** (ERP ledger vouchers: Account_Code__c → Account, VR_Date__c, Dramt__c debit, Cramt__c credit, Due_Date__c) and **Allocation_Transactions__c** (receipts matched to invoices: ACC_Code__c → Account, Alloc_Amount__c). Few records; Account.Ledger_Balance__c is the quickest outstanding figure.

**Product2** (~166 TMT bars): Name, ProductCode, Family [550D, GREEN, CRS 550D], Is_Parent__c, Parent_Product__c, Size__c.

**Influencer__c** (~165): Influencer_Type__c [Architect, Mason, Barbendor, Contractor, Builder, Engineer, …], Status__c [Draft, Active], Influencer_Category__c [ARS, Dealer], MDE__c, Dealer__c, Region__c, Total_Loyalty_Points__c, Available_Loyalty_Points__c. **Loyalty_Request__c** / **Redemption_Request__c**: Approval_Status__c [New, In Approval, Approved, Rejected], points.

**Scheme__c** (Category__c [Direct Growth, Tonnage, FTS], Status__c, From_date__c, Upto_Date__c), **Scheme_Account__c** (dealer enrolment: Scheme__c, Account__c, Total_Quantity__c). **Branding_Request__c** (Request_From__c → Account, Status__c [New, Delivered, Partially Delivered, Cancelled]). **Case** (AccountId, Type mostly Order Related, Status [New, Closed, …], Priority). **Manager_MOM__c** (MOM_Date__c, MOM_Type__c, Executive__c). **PJP_Plan__c** (Executive__c, Frequency__c, Is_Active__c). **Fiscal_Week__c** (April–March fiscal weeks).

**User** (~43 logins): Name, IsActive, Department, Title, LastLoginDate. LoginHistory (LoginTime, UserId) counts login events, not people; for "how many people logged in today" count User with LastLoginDate = TODAY (Salesforce logins) or Employee__c with Last_Login__c = TODAY (field app).

Almost empty or unused, don''t build answers on them: Telecallers__c (0), Order_Line__c, Credit_Limit_Master__c, Dealer_Staff__c, Contact (few), Opportunity (demo data, not real sales), Tech_Van__c (all "New").

## 4. Data traps (always apply)
- **Outliers:** a few Secondary_Order__c records have Quantity_in_MT__c of 10,000 to trillions (test data), and one collection amount is 5,000,000,000,000. When summing tonnage or money, add a filter such as Quantity_in_MT__c < 10000 (or Collected_Amount__c < 100000000) and say that test values were left out.
- **Use the status values listed above as they appear in the data** (e.g. "Submitted For Approval", "Open - Not Contacted", "Pending" exist although they aren''t in the picklist setup).
- Visit status is Visit_Status__c; site status is Site_Status__c.
- Two objects are labelled "Competitor": Competitor__c (brand list) and Dealer_Competitor__c (competitor stock seen at a dealer or site).
- Same-label fields: Order.Manager__c (→ Employee__c) and Order.Approver_Manager__c (→ User) are both "Manager"; prefer Manager__c. Region_Master__c.Amount__c is the travel rate per km, not sales.
- Many ERP pushes failed (Order_Punch_Status__c = ''Failed''); invoices are far fewer than orders. Mention this when comparing orders with invoices.
- Most CO orders are "CO Expired". For live business use DO statuses or recent dates.

## 5. Recipes for common questions
- **Executives logged in today, by region:** Employee__c, filter Last_Login__c = TODAY (and Status__c = ''Active''), group by Region_Master__c.
- **Present today / attendance by region:** Attendance__c, filter Attendance_Date__c = TODAY, group by Region__c then Attendance_Type__c.
- **Secondary orders today by region and status, with tonnes:** Secondary_Order__c, filter CreatedDate = TODAY (or Order_date__c = TODAY) and Quantity_in_MT__c < 10000, group by Region__c then Status__c, aggregate SUM of Quantity_in_MT__c (count comes with it).
- **Conversion rate:** Secondary_Order__c count with Status__c = ''Converted'' ÷ all (excluding Draft and Cancelled), for the period asked.
- **Dealer 360 (by dealer code):** Account where Customer_Code__c = the code (Name, Account_Type__c, Status__c, Region__c, Customer_Credit_Risk__c, Credit_Limit__c, Ledger_Balance__c, Payment_Due_Date__c, Pending_Order_Amount__c, Current_Year_Target__c, Current_Year_Actual__c, Current_Month_SSS__c, Previous_Month_SSS__c). Then, filtering by that dealer: Order (AccountId; group by Status or Type; SUM Total_Quantity__c), Secondary_Order__c (Dealer_Distributor__c; group by Status__c; SUM Quantity_in_MT__c < 10000), Invoice__c (Dealer_Distributor__c; SUM Total_Invoice_Amount__c, Total_Weight_in_MT__c; by month of Invoice_Date__c), Dealer_Target__c (Dealer__c; Target__c vs Achieved_Target__c), Collection_Plan__c (Customer_Dealer_Distributor__c; Estimated vs Collected), Current_Stock__c (Dealer__c; Total_Stock_in_MT__c by Item__c), Visit__c (Account__c; recent visits by Visit_Status__c), Case (AccountId; open cases), Scheme_Account__c (Account__c). A lookup can be filtered by the dealer''s record name, so filter Order.AccountId = the dealer''s Name or Id.
- **Target vs achievement:** Dealer_Target__c (tonnage) or Employee_Target__c grouped by Target_Type__c; achievement % = Achieved_Target__c ÷ Target__c.
- **Visits by executive or region:** Visit__c, filter Visit_date__c for the period, group by Executive__c or Region_Master__c then Visit_Status__c.
- **Site pipeline:** Site_Lead__c grouped by Site_Status__c or Type_of_Building__c, SUM Total_Estimated_Steel_Requirement_MT__c.
- **Collections:** Collection_Plan__c for the period, SUM Estimated_Amount__c and Collected_Amount__c (outlier filter), group by Executive__c or Status__c.
- **Stock at dealers:** Current_Stock__c grouped by Dealer__c or Item__c, SUM Total_Stock_in_MT__c.

## 6. How to present
- Money in Indian style (₹, lakh, crore) and steel in MT. Dates as "26 Oct 2026".
- Say which date field a "today" or period figure is based on when it matters (created vs order date).
- Never show Aadhaar, PAN, bank details, passwords or session ids (they are blocked anyway), and don''t list people''s phone numbers or emails unless the person asks for one specific contact.
- ERP data that isn''t in Salesforce (full ledger, production, dispatch weights beyond invoices) isn''t available here; say so in one line and answer the rest.', u.id
FROM users u
JOIN user_roles ur ON ur.user_id = u.id
JOIN roles r ON r.id = ur.role_id
WHERE r.code = 'SUPER_ADMIN'
  AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM ai_rules WHERE chat_mode = 'SALESFORCE')
ORDER BY u.id
LIMIT 1
-- @end
